{"id": "EUVD-2026-102527", "enisaUuid": "a1540a58-1f89-3b43-9c6d-b3cd862b4472", "description": "LibRaw through 0.22.2 contains a heap-based out-of-bounds read in LibRaw::parseNikonMakernote() that allows attackers to read past a short ShotInfo buffer. Attackers can supply a crafted Nikon NEF/TIFF with a 5-byte ShotInfo tag declaring version 243 to crash applications decoding the image.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:09:25", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libraw-nikon-shotinfo-orientationoffset-oob-read", "https://github.com/LibRaw/LibRaw/blob/b93f6e45c194f5df9b02a43b1af9a54b4f41f33f/src/metadata/nikon.cpp#L873-L967", "https://github.com/LibRaw/LibRaw", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libraw-through-0.22.2-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-parsenikonmakernote-shotinfo"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7w2h-vp67-rpcv", "CVE-2026-111272"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7e8e8d6c-a0c1-39d4-af6c-b3a2a9a088de", "product": {"name": "LibRaw", "vendor": {"name": "LibRaw"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.22.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f30a5825-2d1c-3164-8bc5-34faad00148a", "vendor": {"name": "LibRaw"}}], "isExploited": false}